/*
 * CPUNET emulator boot-parity FLASH enlargement.
 *
 * DO NOT read this as the real device flash map. The physical nRF5340 network
 * core has 256 KiB of FLASH (0x01000000 + 256K) and the shipped netcore image
 * (225,632 B, loaded at runtime base 0x01008800) fits it with 1,696 B spare.
 *
 * Our cohesive recovered build is ~2.3 KiB larger than the shipped image
 * because it links lean recovered code alongside separately-compiled SDK
 * archives (a recovered<->SDK duplication residual). The physical link is
 * symbol-clean (0 undefined, 0 duplicate) but its image span (~227,961 B)
 * overflows the real usable region (256K - 0x8800 = 227,328 B) by 633 B.
 *
 * The linker derives the FLASH region as
 *   ORIGIN = CONFIG_FLASH_BASE_ADDRESS + CONFIG_FLASH_LOAD_OFFSET  (0x01008800)
 *   LENGTH = CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE*1K - CONFIG_FLASH_LOAD_OFFSET
 * and CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE is derived from this flash1 reg size. Modeling a
 * slightly larger net flash therefore grows LENGTH WITHOUT moving the load
 * base 0x01008800 (which is mandatory: the net image is position-DEPENDENT).
 *
 * 256K -> 260K adds 4 KiB (two 2048 B erase blocks) of usable FLASH:
 *   usable = 260*1024 - 0x8800 = 231,424 B  (was 227,328 B)
 * which fits the cohesive image with headroom. This is a deliberate
 * emulator-vs-device divergence to unblock emulator bring-up. Real-device fit
 * requires eliminating the recovered<->SDK duplication (byte-match endgame),
 * tracked separately, NOT done here. See FLASH_DIVERGENCE.md.
 */

&flash1 {
	reg = <0x01000000 DT_SIZE_K(260)>;
};
